{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_2>\nimport sys\nimport bisect\n\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\nn, m = int(data[0]), int(data[1])\na = [int(x) % m for x in data[2:2+n]]\n\ndef subset_sums_modulo(arr, mod):\n    sums = {0}\n    for val in arr:\n        new_sums = set()\n        for s in sums:\n            new_sums.add((s + val) % mod)\n            new_sums.add(s)\n        sums = new_sums\n    return sums\n\nmid = n // 2\nleft = subset_sums_modulo(a[:mid], m)\nright = subset_sums_modulo(a[mid:], m)\n\nright_list = sorted(right)\nbest = 0\n\nfor s in left:\n    needed = m - s\n    pos = bisect.bisect_left(right_list, needed)\n    for offset in [-1, 0]:\n        if 0 <= pos + offset < len(right_list):\n            total = s + right_list[pos + offset]\n            if total > best:\n                best = total\n\nprint(best)\n</your_rewritten_code_2>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <set>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cctype>\n#include <string>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nvector<int> subset_sums_modulo(const vector<int>& arr, int mod) {\n    set<int> sums;\n    sums.insert(0);\n    for (int val : arr) {\n        set<int> new_sums;\n        for (int s : sums) {\n            new_sums.insert((s + val) % mod);\n            new_sums.insert(s);\n        }\n        sums = new_sums;\n    }\n    return vector<int>(sums.begin(), sums.end());\n}\n\nint main() {\n    string input;\n    getline(cin, input);\n    \n    vector<string> data;\n    string current = \"\";\n    for (char c : input) {\n        if (c == ' ' || c == '\\t' || c == '\\n') {\n            if (!current.empty()) {\n                data.push_back(current);\n                current = \"\";\n            }\n        } else {\n            current += c;\n        }\n    }\n    if (!current.empty()) {\n        data.push_back(current);\n    }\n    \n    int n = stoi(data[0]);\n    int m = stoi(data[1]);\n    \n    vector<int> a;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        a.push_back(stoi(data[2 + i]) % m);\n    }\n    \n    vector<int> left_sums = subset_sums_modulo(vector<int>(a.begin(), a.begin() + n/2), m);\n    vector<int> right_sums = subset_sums_modulo(vector<int>(a.begin() + n/2, a.end()), m);\n    \n    sort(right_sums.begin(), right_sums.end());\n    \n    int best = 0;\n    for (int s : left_sums) {\n        int needed = m - s;\n        auto pos = lower_bound(right_sums.begin(), right_sums.end(), needed);\n        \n        for (int offset = -1; offset <= 0; offset++) {\n            int idx = pos - right_sums.begin() + offset;\n            if (idx >= 0 && idx < (int)right_sums.size()) {\n                int total = s + right_sums[idx];\n                if (total > best) {\n                    best = total;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << best << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00014649749209638685, -1.668928689468